+1. **P1 — `profile?: ReactNode` cannot reliably determine whether a badge rendered.** [plan:53](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/docs/plans/261002e-mode-corner-icons-and-gutter-icon-polish.md:53), [WrittenForYou.tsx:128](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/WrittenForYou.tsx:128), [IdeasPanel.tsx:204](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/IdeasPanel.tsx:204), [Tweets.tsx:114](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/Tweets.tsx:114). Ideas and Tweets can pass a real `<WrittenForYou>` element which subsequently returns `null`; `ModeSurface` would still see a truthy node, add `.has-profile`, and reserve space for an absent badge. Fix by either pre-gating every call site on the actual profiled condition, or more simply derive the expanded room in CSS with `:has(.band-corner > .prof-badge)`. Add both profiled and unprofiled fixtures; the proposed “any badge is in the corner” assertion can otherwise pass vacuously.
+
+2. **P1 — the existing coarse-pointer minimum will prevent the proposed 32px badge.** [narrow-window.css:861](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/styles/narrow-window.css:861), [profile.css:440](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/styles/profile.css:440). Setting `width`/`height: 2rem` does not override `.prof-badge.icon-only { min-width/min-height: 2.5rem }`, so the main phone defect remains. Explicitly remove or scope that rule away from the corner, reset both minimum dimensions, and remove the border there. A `corner` prop is unnecessary if `.band-corner .prof-badge` owns the appearance.
+
+3. **P1 — “every top row already clears” is only horizontally true; moving the badge can collapse the row vertically.** [plan:69](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/docs/plans/261002e-mode-corner-icons-and-gutter-icon-polish.md:69), [GlossaryPanel.tsx:336](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/GlossaryPanel.tsx:336), [QuotesPanel.tsx:726](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/QuotesPanel.tsx:726), [IdeasPanel.tsx:187](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/IdeasPanel.tsx:187). In the no-sort Glossary/Quotes states and in Ideas, the badge is the only possible header content. Removing it leaves an empty `.band-head` roughly one padding-row high, while the coarse corner reaches 32px plus its top inset; deleting that header instead lets the corner overlap the first status/list row. Specify a corner-only minimum block size or an explicit host row for these states, and test loading, one-item, unprofiled, and profiled states. Summary and Tweets already have real control rows.
+
