+
+8. **P2 — one `data-tip` string is not enough to render a `ControlTip`, and blindly describing labelled buttons duplicates speech.** [plan:94](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/docs/plans/261002e-mode-corner-icons-and-gutter-icon-polish.md:94), [Tooltip.tsx:388](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icons/src/web/Tooltip.tsx:388), [BlockLinkCard.tsx:277](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhf4svm-mode-header-and-gutter-icon-polish/src/web/BlockLinkCard.tsx:277). `ControlTip` requires a heading plus `what` and `how`; several proposed strings exactly equal the button’s `aria-label`, so attaching them as `aria-describedby` may announce the same sentence twice. Use `TipNote` for the current one-line copy, or define genuinely additional `what/how` data. Skip `aria-describedby` where the tooltip adds nothing to the accessible name. Ensure `.blk-cmt` joins the delegated selector too.
